OL,4,CBBC apologises for 'any offence        
OL,5,Ccaused' by Strictly noise disruption   
OL,6,GThe BBC has apologised "for any        
OL,7,Goffence caused" after lewd audio was   
OL,8,Gheard during the live broadcast of     
OL,9,GStrictly Come Dancing.                 
OL,11,FA recording of sex noises appeared to  
OL,12,Fbe playing from the audience in        
OL,13,FBlackpool's Tower Ballroom as judge    
OL,14,FMotsi Mabuse gave feedback early in    
OL,15,FSaturday's episode. She paused before  
OL,16,Fjoking: "It's not me."                 
OL,22,                                   G2/4 
OL,23,D]CNews IndexG102CFlashG150CRegionalG160
